Expected elements: present

Presence check passes at 1920x1080. Provenance banner (badge, "Synthetic demo data", chain slug `aztec`, four producer sentences) sits above a slim identity bar carrying the truncated hash, `Partial`, block 101, an exit to the chain, both stepping directions, the scrubber, phase rail and the NOIR tag. Code pane is positioned at line 32 with a run marker; Call Trace and Event Log are one tab strip with Call Trace open and seven frames; Values is a separate pane below with eleven rows; the Transaction pane carries identity. No spinner, no empty pane, no light chrome, no removed loading paragraph, no Values tab.

Through the density lens the panes themselves are well packed — 23px code rows, a right-aligned opcode column, 25px value rows — but the vertical budget is misallocated. The centre column carries roughly 310px of dead space (about 250px below the last call frame, another 60px under the last value row) while both neighbours are truncated: Code clips lines 40 and 53 flush against x≈912 with no ellipsis or scroll affordance, and the Transaction pane is cut mid-JSON at the viewport edge and wraps FEE PAYER and TARGET across two lines mid-hex. The banner takes 185px (17% of the viewport) to set a four-line paragraph to a 370px measure inside a 1920px band that is otherwise empty.

Highest-priority fixes: give the centre column's slack to Code or Transaction, and set the banner prose to a wide measure so it costs two lines instead of four.

Rating: 7/10

